# The script the fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which binds every key of the Vim scheme's `C-w`
# table with `bindKey`, so the window commands are reached in insert state
# without leaving it. What it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches
# no file.

reload
settle
resize 640 480

# `C-w v` splits view 0. Under master-and-stack the new window, view 1, goes
# right after it in the list, so it is the stack, on the right, and focused.
# `i` begins an insert in it, and `ab` is typed.
key w KeyW control
key v KeyV -
key i KeyI -
commit ab

# `C-w h` in insert state focuses the window on the left, view 0, main.
key w KeyW control
key h KeyH -
scene

# `C-w l` focuses view 1 again, which is still in insert state.
key w KeyW control
key l KeyL -
scene

# `c` is typed after `ab`: both views show `abc`.
commit c
scene
